Investigate a historical change (@pathway-investigate-a-historical-change: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_1GP5K0FT8V18QN96V80XDSBVEY
Place this route under History and connect the selected question to Sociology, Political-Economy, Philosophy, or Literature. Choose a bounded change in a society, institution, practice, economy, or body of ideas. Introduce chronology, source origin, context, and comparison of accounts alongside the investigation. An object or technical practice can be one entrance into the broader historical question.

Join selected sources and scholarship through a concise evidenced account. Compare interpretations, identify missing or conflicting evidence, and make the proposed causal explanation explicit. Ask how period, place, perspective, and the survival of sources affect the account, and what further evidence could strengthen or challenge it.

**Related plans:** [History](../../scholazein/history/History.lingua#r_3MKG6XS2X0W9YR8T4438CTGZ1T), [Sociology](../../scholazein/sociology/Sociology.lingua#r_2ENBJ86RED2J0TCGJFZARTTNQT), [Political-Economy](../../scholazein/political-economy/Political-Economy.lingua#r_2WPG1Y767BM24Z0K4BY6Y6T62W), [Philosophical study](../../scholazein/philosophy/Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001), [Literature](../../scholazein/literature/Literature.lingua#r_68XTEFTFVR5ZPB68D6E1XK0SR3).

